# Cilium's eBPF/kube-proxy-replacement needs real host capabilities that
# rootless Podman's user namespace can't grant — cluster creation runs
# under `sudo` (rootful Podman) instead, so no env vars are needed here.
# `kind create cluster` takes `KIND_EXPERIMENTAL_PROVIDER=podman` inline on
# the sudo command line (see the `cluster` Makefile target) since exported
# vars aren't preserved across `sudo` by default.
#
# kubectl/helm/cilium/argocd only talk to the API server over the network
# and use the default ~/.kube/config — no special env needed for them.
